{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: rewrote the per-observation likelihood loop `y[n] ~ bernoulli_logit(...)` into a single top-level protected observation statement `y ~ bernoulli_logit(eta)`. The local model-block vector `eta` is computed deterministically from already-prior-sampled parameters and context data (`jj`, `kk`, `N`). This preserves the same Bernoulli-logit likelihood while satisfying SafeStan's requirement that protected data appear exactly once on the left side of a plain sampling statement outside loops. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"// IRT 1PL (RASCH) MODEL 

data {
  int<lower=1> J; // number of students
  int<lower=1> K; // number of questions
  int<lower=1> N; // number of observations
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> jj; // student for observation n
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> kk; // question for observation n
  array[N] int<lower=0, upper=1> y; // correctness for observation n
}
parameters {
  real delta; // mean student ability
  array[J] real alpha; // ability of student j - mean ability
  array[K] real beta; // difficulty of question k
}
model {
  vector[N] eta;

  alpha ~ normal(0, 1); // informative true prior
  beta ~ normal(0, 1); // informative true prior
  delta ~ normal(.75, 1); // informative true prior

  for (n in 1 : N) {
    eta[n] = alpha[jj[n]] - beta[kk[n]] + delta;
  }
  y ~ bernoulli_logit(eta);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":4,"K":1,"N":2,"jj":[4,1],"kk":[1,1],"y":[0,0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
